From: Soultaco83 <soulnacho@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 24 Sep 2026 00:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Fix login page DOMPurify ReferenceError

The login controller references `createDOMPurify()` but only imports the
default `DOMPurify` export from `dompurify`. dompurify 2.5.9 does not
export `createDOMPurify` as a named export, so the identifier is undefined
at runtime and the login page fails with:

    ReferenceError: createDOMPurify is not defined

The default export is itself a callable factory, so call it directly to
obtain a dedicated instance. This preserves the intent of scoping the
relaxed ALLOWED_URI_REGEXP to the login disclaimer without mutating the
shared default instance used by other sanitize call sites.

diff --git a/src/apps/legacy/controllers/session/login/index.js b/src/apps/legacy/controllers/session/login/index.js
index 914e2b03bd..f8eaf3bb44 100644
--- a/src/apps/legacy/controllers/session/login/index.js
+++ b/src/apps/legacy/controllers/session/login/index.js
@@ -23,7 +23,7 @@ import { getDefaultBackgroundClass } from 'components/cardbuilder/utils/builder'
 
 import './login.scss';
 
-const domPurify = createDOMPurify();
+const domPurify = DOMPurify();
 domPurify.setConfig({
     // eslint-disable-next-line @typescript-eslint/naming-convention, sonarjs/regex-complexity -- DOMPurify config option; customizes its default regex
     ALLOWED_URI_REGEXP: /^(?:(?:https?|mailto|tel|callto|cid|xmpp|matrix|tg|whatsapp|signal|ircs?):|[^a-z]|[a-z+.-]+(?:[^-a-z+.:]|$))/i
